  * Vsync (notification type 5) sends (timestamp, timestamp, 0) as 32-bit
  * halves to clients that enabled it. The panel memory itself is published
  * as an IOSurface and returned as the default framebuffer surface. The
- * kernel text console keeps drawing over the GUI by default: pausing it
- * (boot-arg kebabfb_noconsole=1, on the first present) mutes the console,
- * which also hides panics.
+ * normal text console hands the GOP to the first validated full BGRA frame
+ * in measured CPU-framebuffer mode (-cf). The USB tee remains active and
+ * the existing panic_active() console exception still displays panic text.
+ * Explicit kebabfb_noconsole=0 keeps the development screen console.
  */
 #include "KebabSurface.h"
 #include <kern/kebab_capture.h>
